All five QA tasks are done:

1. **`validate`/`test`/`build`** all passed cleanly with no fixes needed.
2. **Bug review** — found and fixed one real defensive gap: `ProfileForm` only checked for an empty grade string, then called `onSubmit` with raw `grade`/`scale`, and `App.jsx` called `toGPA` uncaught — any value that made `toGPA` throw (blank/partial-number strings, an unrecognized letter grade) would crash the whole app with no error boundary. I moved the `toGPA` conversion + try/catch into `ProfileForm`, so it now surfaces a friendly inline error instead of white-screening, and `App.jsx` only ever receives an already-valid `{ gpa, interests }`. Everything else checked out already: `match.js` guards interest-fit division by zero, out-of-range numeric grades clamp instead of erroring, and contradictory cost filters (`maxTotalCost` below available tuition) already degrade gracefully to a "no results / relax filters" empty state rather than crashing. I extracted the inline filter/sort logic from `App.jsx` into `src/lib/filters.js` so it's unit-testable, and extended `scripts/test-match.mjs` from 8 to 19 assertions covering NaN/blank/partial-number inputs, letter-grade case/whitespace/near-miss edge cases, label boundary conditions, zero-interest-overlap scoring, and contradictory-filter/empty-sort regressions.
3. **README.md** added — what the app is, a screenshot placeholder note, the match-score formula and label thresholds, run instructions, and Vercel deploy steps.
4. **`vercel.json`** added (SPA rewrite to `index.html`) and **`.gitignore`** expanded (env files, editor dirs, `.vercel`, etc.), while keeping the existing `prompts/`, `recordings/`, `transcripts/` content tracked since it looked like intentional project material rather than build output.
5. **Git initialized**, branch renamed to `main`, secrets-scanned before staging, and committed everything (except `node_modules`/`dist`) in one conventional-style initial commit.
